    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q23-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $c=\\dfrac{ab}{h}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c=\\dfrac{ab}{h}$.\n\nEquate the areas $\\tfrac12ch$ and $\\tfrac12ab$.",
          "worked": "Express the triangle's area using its perpendicular legs and using the hypotenuse with its altitude:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{ch}{2}&=\\frac{ab}{2}\\\\\nch&=ab\\\\\nc&=\\frac{ab}{h}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The **Inverse Pythagorean Theorem** states that\n$$\\frac{1}{a^2}+\\frac{1}{b^2}=\\frac{1}{h^2}.$$\nProve this result.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{a^2}+\\dfrac{1}{b^2}=\\dfrac{1}{h^2}$.\n\nUse $a^2+b^2=c^2$ and $c=\\frac{ab}{h}$ from part (a).",
          "worked": "By Pythagoras, $a^2+b^2=c^2$. Part (a) gives $\\frac{c}{(ab)}=\\frac{1}{h}$. Therefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{1}{a^2}+\\frac{1}{b^2}&=\\frac{a^2+b^2}{a^2b^2}\\\\\n\\frac{1}{a^2}+\\frac{1}{b^2}&=\\frac{c^2}{a^2b^2}\\\\\n\\frac{1}{a^2}+\\frac{1}{b^2}&=\\left(\\frac{c}{ab}\\right)^2\\\\\n\\frac{1}{a^2}+\\frac{1}{b^2}&=\\frac{1}{h^2}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
